 "v3_rules": {
  "E1": "Charge-normalisation literals. (c) also fires on a hypothesis that references a tier-Q SM variable and contains a standalone integer literal n with |n| in sm_int_literals_hyp (3, 4, 6: the distinctive values of the integer x6 form Q=1, u^c=-4, d^c=2, L=-3, e^c=6, H=3 and of the integer Y/2 form). Standalone = not part of a fraction, not an exponent, not glued to an identifier. Fractions: v2's yQ=1/6 list (sm_literals_hyp, unchanged) plus sm_literals_hyp_E1 = 4/3 (Q=T3+Y/2: Y(u_R)=4/3; 1/3, 2/3, 1/2 already listed). Tier-C variables are exempt: kinematic integers in coupling statements (EWZ1b.forced) are not charges.",
  "E2": "N_c-symbolic normalisation. (c) also fires on a hypothesis in which one multiplicative term contains both an nc_vars variable and a charge_vars variable (2*N_c*yQ, N_c*yQ: the ACC-with-fixed-yL relation of FRMU/STRUCT2 in Y and Y/2 conventions) or which divides by an nc_vars variable (1/(2*N_c), 1/N_c).",
  "E3": "D1 tightened. A binder bound to an SM-var structure (D1) makes the statement SM-structure only if the conclusion reads an SM-var constant (a coupling or charge field such as x.a); a conclusion that only mentions x (kinematic fields) is not SM-structure. D1's unconstrained-identity rule for field reads is unchanged."
 },
 "sm_literals_hyp_E1": [
  "4/3",
  "-4/3"
 ]
